 "evidenceBoundary": {
  "exact": "The selected installed native inputs, upstream grouped layer record and tile dispatcher contracts, all listed UnityPlayer .pdata windows and their complete SHA256 windows, record-to-handle staging, owner forwarding, three copy pairings, guards, destination-handle getter, lower-level copy-routine call, property-name literals, property-ID stores and render-binding calls are checked.",
  "direct": "The selected dispatcher takes the grouped LAYER record from its own queue. Its three path-result slots are resolved in D/N/C order, forwarded through the owner consumer, and paired with three distinct owner-local resource handles. The same three handles are paired with string-derived render-property IDs: D to _Splats, N to _Normals, and C to _ConeMaps.",
  "conditional": "The owner consumer can decline a record before the copy dispatcher. The third copy also requires a present source and an available destination; its render binding skips a null resource. The common helper can skip the lower-level copy call when source and destination properties differ; the lower-level routine has its own guards.",
